{"passage": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, carries genetic instructions for all living organisms. It is shaped like a double helix and was first described by James Watson and Francis Crick in 1953. This discovery unlocked the secrets of heredity and evolution.", "question": "Who first described the structure of DNA?", "answers": [{"text": "James Watson and Francis Crick", "label": 1}, {"text": "Albert Einstein", "label": 0}, {"text": "Charles Darwin", "label": 0}]}
{"passage": "The Olympic Games originated in ancient Greece around 776 BC as a religious festival. Modern Olympics began in 1896 in Athens and include summer and winter events. Athletes compete in various sports to win gold medals.", "question": "When did the modern Olympic Games begin?", "answers": [{"text": "1896 in Athens", "label": 1}, {"text": "776 BC", "label": 0}, {"text": "1900 in Paris", "label": 0}]}
